<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Addac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 418</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Addax</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Addax was king of the Alans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, who had crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> and Suebi in 406 and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 409. The Alans settled in Lusitania and Carthaginiensis. From 416 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wallia">Wallia</a>, acting for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, campaigned against them, and in 418 Addax was killed and his people crushed; the survivors joined the Hasding Vandals under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunderic">Gunderic</a>.</p></div>
